course: dictionary
lesson: 2142
title: Coping with hard things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cope is a verb: cope, copes, coped, coping. It means to deal well with something hard and keep going. «Fostering is looking after a child from another family for a while, when their own parents cannot cope for now.» Cannot cope means they cannot manage the hard situation for now.
explain: Cope is often followed by with, as in cope with a problem or cope with work. «People grieve in different ways; some need normal things like playing and laughing to cope.» Here cope means getting through a sad time.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a word like manage or get through and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Cope means to deal well with a hard problem or situation, and to keep going.
fact: To cope with work or a job means to manage to do it.
fact: «Can't cope» means something feels too hard to manage.
fact: Coping skills are ways of dealing with worry, anger, change or loss, such as talking to someone, breathing slowly or taking a break.
fact: The past tense of cope is coped, and the -ing form is coping.
exercise: «Fostering is looking after a child from another family for a while, when their own parents cannot cope for now.» What does cannot cope mean here? | Cannot remember the family's name | Cannot stop laughing | *Cannot manage the hard situation for now | Cannot find their car keys
exercise: «Some need normal things like playing and laughing to cope.» Which phrase could replace cope without changing the meaning? | *Get through the hard time | Shout loudly | Forget everything | Go to sleep forever
exercise: Which word is the past tense of cope? | coping | cop | *coped | copes
test: Ahmed says, «I can't cope with my maths homework.» What does he mean? | He loves his maths homework | He has finished all of it | He has lost his pencil | *He can't find a way to manage it
test: Which is a good coping skill when you feel angry? | *Take a slow breath and then take a break | Ignore everyone forever | Slam the door and shout | Break something on purpose
exam: Complete the sentence: «Children learn ways to ___ with worry, anger and change.» | *cope | cop | copy | cup
